<title>BELGIUM: Boeing merger decision still set for July 23 - EC.</title>
<headline>Boeing merger decision still set for July 23 - EC.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday that July 23 remained its target date for a decision on whether or not to clear Boeing's planned merger with former U.S. rival McDonnell Douglas , a spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;According to all appearances, the 23rd of July is the date,&quot; the spokesman said in response to reporters' questions.</p>
<p>His remarks follow a unanimous decision on Friday by national competition officials in the 15 EU states to back the Commission's recommendation to block the planned merger in its current form.</p>
<p>The spokesman said national competition authorities could be consulted in writing on their thoughts on any compromise struck between EU regulators and Boeing executives to make the deal acceptable.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
